From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 13:11:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05312/11362] [outer-loop] retract ARC value-head distillation
 task: exp4652 already tried and nulled it

Item 1b of 2 shovel-ready tasks ('fix the roadmap collision, 1 then 2').

Before building the distillation this task called for, checked whether
exp4652 (previously cited as ONLY testing call-frequency reduction) also
covered cost-per-call reduction. It did: exp4652 already used
cross_game_features_v3_value_routing (arc_value_learner.py:462), a
pre-existing cheap feature variant that skips the expensive
_object_relational_features step -- its own docstring says those features
'were measured as dead weight for live routing'. exp4652's measured cost:
0.397ms/node.

Measured the true precondition-(a) baseline on the real Kaggle sandbox
(kernel carnot-arc-cgf3-diag): full cross_game_features_v3 = 4283.53us/call,
8.8x the component-stats sub-step alone. exp4652's already-tried distilled
subset (397us/call) is ~10.8x faster -- a genuine order-of-magnitude
speedup, clearing this task's own gate for re-running the live A/B.
exp4652 ALREADY ran that A/B: live_lift_ci=[0.0, 0.0], an exact zero-width
null. Building a new distillation experiment would have been a doomed
rerun of exp4652 under a different name -- caught before building.

Net: all five sub-hypotheses on the selection/value-head axis (representation,
distribution-shift, calibration, call-frequency, cost-per-call) are now
exhausted and nulled. Retiring the axis; redirecting future ARC effort to
the generation axis (the actual open headroom).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
